msgstr ":math:`\\rho_{H_2O} =` densidad del agua"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:210
msgid ":math:`g =` acceleration due to gravity"
msgstr ":math:`g =` aceleración debida a la gravedad"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:211
msgid ":math:`C_D =` drag coefficient"
msgstr ":math:`C_D =` coeficiente de arrastre"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:212
msgid ":math:`v_t=` particle terminal velocity"
msgstr ":math:`v_t=` velocidad terminal de partícula"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:213
msgid ":math:`D=` particle diameter"
msgstr ":math:`D=` diámetro de las partículas"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:215
msgid "Plugging into the original force balance,"
msgstr "Conectando al equilibrio de fuerzas original,"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:217
msgid ""
"\\left [C_D A_{floc} \\rho_{H_2O} \\frac{v_t^2}{2} \\right]+\\left "
"[\\forall_{floc} \\rho_{H_2O} g\\right ]-\\left [\\forall_{floc} "
"\\rho_{floc} g \\right] =0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:221
#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:750
msgid "Solving for terminal velocity, :math:`v_t`, we obtain"
msgstr "Resolviendo para la velocidad terminal, :math:`v_t`, obtenemos"

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:223
msgid ""
"v_t = \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}\\frac{g "
"D_{floc}}{C_D}\\frac{(\\rho_{floc}-\\rho_{H_2O})}{\\rho_{H_2O}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:228
msgid ""
"Terminal velocity is a function of fluid density, floc density, gravity, "
"particle diameter, and the drag coefficient. To calculate velocity, all of "
"those inputs must be determined."
msgstr ""
"La velocidad terminal es función de la densidad del fluido, la densidad de "
"flocas, la gravedad, el diámetro de la partícula y el coeficiente de "
"arrastre. Para calcular la velocidad, deben determinarse todas esas "
"entradas."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:230
msgid ""
"The first component that we will focus on is the drag coefficient, "
":math:`C_D`. The drag coefficient is function of Reynolds Number, "
":math:`Re`, and the characteristic flow around a particle. As a reminder, "
":math:`Re = \\frac{v_t D_{floc}}{\\nu}` where :math:`v_t` is the velocity of"
" the fluid relative to the particle, :math:`D_{floc}` is the characteristic "
"length scale (in this case the floc diameter), and :math:`\\nu` is kinematic"
" viscosity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:232
msgid ""
"Drag coefficients are used to describe flow around a particle and are shown "
"in :numref:`figure_drag_coeff_Re_base`."
msgstr ""
"Los coeficientes de arrastre se utilizan para describir el flujo alrededor "
"de una partícula y se muestran en :numref:`figure_drag_coeff_Re_base`."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:241
#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:267
msgid "Drag coefficient as a function of Reynolds number."
msgstr "Coeficiente de arrastre en función del número de Reynolds."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:241
msgid "Drag coefficient on a sphere as a function of Reynolds number."
msgstr "Coeficiente de arrastre en una esfera en función del número de Reynolds."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:243
msgid ""
"As an introduction to this drag coefficient diagram, we can compare it to "
"something we've already learned about: the Moody diagram. Drawing parallels "
"between the two will help us understand some important relationships better."
msgstr ""
"Como introducción a este diagrama de coeficientes de arrastre, podemos "
"compararlo con algo que ya hemos aprendido: el diagrama de Moody. Establecer"
" paralelismos entre ambos nos ayudará a entender mejor algunas relaciones "
"importantes."

#: ../../Flocs_Fractals_and_Forces/FFF_Intro.rst:247
msgid "Comparison of the Moody diagram and the Drag Coefficient diagram."
msgstr "Comparación del diagrama de Moody y el diagrama del coeficiente de arrastre."

